Docs are written and the changelog has a **2.4.0** entry. A client walks the list like this:

```ts
let cursor: string | undefined;
do {
  const page = await orders.list({ cursor });
  render(page.data);
  cursor = page.next_cursor ?? undefined;
} while (cursor);
```

- `limit` defaults to 50, at most 100
- `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page

The guide is `C:\Users\alice\code\api\docs\pagination.md`, the route is in `C:\Users\alice\code\api\src\routes`. Reference: https://docs.example.com/api/pagination
